# Raw assets waiting to be processed
incoming/*
!incoming/README.md

# Written without a trailing slash on purpose. `dist/` ignores a directory but
# not a symlink of the same name, and these are symlinks — so the first version
# of this file committed them, and an `rm -rf dist` then showed up as deleting
# a tracked file.
#
# ── iCloud ──
# This project lives under ~/Documents, which macOS syncs. A build writing 200
# files while a sync is mid-flight produces conflict copies — "index 2.html",
# "brief 2.php", a second copy of every font — and dist/ is ignored, so nothing
# caught them until 190 of them broke the test run. iCloud skips anything whose
# name ends in .nosync, so the generated directories are real folders with that
# suffix and a symlink under the original name.
#
# node_modules deliberately NOT done this way: Playwright transpiles anything
# outside a literal node_modules/ path, which breaks axe-core.
*.nosync

# The FTP password, and nothing else. The deploy scripts themselves live in
# scripts/ and are versioned — they are how the site ships, so losing them
# to a gitignore on the directory that happened to hold the secret is not a
# trade worth making.
.deploy/credentials
